tasks.details:
In src/sources/types.ts define:
```ts
export interface DataSource<T extends z.ZodTypeAny = z.ZodTypeAny> {
  slug: string;               // e.g. 'uk-planning'
  title: string;
  recordSchema: T;            // zod schema of one normalized record
  fetchFresh(env: CloudflareBindings): Promise<z.infer<T>[]>;
  refresh: { cron: string; cacheTtlSeconds: number };
  queryParams: z.ZodObject<any>; // filters this source supports (validated per-request)
  creditCost?: number;        // default 1
}
```
src/sources/registry.ts: `export const registry: Record<string, DataSource>` + `getSource(slug)` helper + a demo in-memory source for tests until task 3 lands. Dataset-specific logic anywhere outside src/sources/ is a design bug (CLAUDE.md isolation rule).
src/routes/data.ts: `GET /v1/data/:source` — 404 envelope for unknown slug; validate query with `source.queryParams.extend({ page: z.coerce.number().int().min(1).default(1), per_page: z.coerce.number().int().max(100).default(25) })`; read records from cache layer (task 3 supplies real cache; until then call fetchFresh), apply declared filters generically (equality/substring per param type), paginate, respond with envelope `meta: { page, per_page, total, source: slug, last_refreshed_at }`. Also `GET /v1/data` (or `/v1/sources`) listing registry entries with title, slug, freshness, and supported params — this later feeds MCP list_sources.
Keep filtering logic generic (driven by the queryParams schema), never per-dataset.
